# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-trustedpaths-real-registry-flaky — the real-registry TRUSTEDPATHS round trip failed once for one profile, not reproducible
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-11-15

* Symptom

One full =make test= on pfenny (French Windows, over ssh, clautolisp 2.4.14)
failed =trustedpaths-real-registry-round-trip-on-windows= for ONE of the two
AutoCAD profiles:

#+begin_example
Software\Autodesk\AutoCAD\R24.1\ACAD-5101:40C\Profiles\Epure\Variables holds
C:\Users\PPBN02261\AppData\Local\Temp\alfe-trust-test-é-448319\...
#+end_example

The write had reported success for both profiles (the token-length check
passed), and the =<<Profil sans nom>>= profile held the entry.

* Not reproduced

- The same test run alone ten times in a row on pfenny: 10/10 pass.
- A traced trust / read / untrust on both profiles: correct.
- The next full alfe suite on pfenny (2726 checks): 0 failures.
- No AutoCAD, accoreconsole or BricsCAD was running.

* Suspects

- =%run-powershell= is wrapped in =ignore-errors= and =%hkcu-read-value=
  returns NIL on no output, so a PowerShell launch that failed under load
  reads as "the entry is absent" -- indistinguishable, in the old message,
  from a real miss.
- A concurrent read-modify-write of the same profile by another process.

* Also seen

=<<Profil sans nom>>= still holds =C:\msys64\tmp\alfe-trust-test-é-956769\...=,
left by an earlier run that never reached its untrust (a test entry the stale
sweep does not recognise, since it is not an alfe-generated workdir name).

* Next

2.4.15 makes the assertion print the value read back. On the next
occurrence, that value says which suspect it is: NIL means the PowerShell
read failed (then make the read retry, or distinguish failure from absence);
a value without the entry means something rewrote the profile.
